        {
            "guidStr": "f09837b1-e6b1-4d0c-9d43-63e8e16b8e59",
            "name": [
                "Name",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                ""
            ],
            "isLive": false,
            "metadata": "",
            "deleted": false,
            "type": "Body",
            "topMarginOverride": -1,
            "bottomMarginOverride": -1,
            "leftMarginOverride": -1,
            "rightMarginOverride": -1,
            "title": [
                "",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                ""
            ],
            "body": [
                "Krueger knew this creature. It led a small cult devoted to Blighterghast, and its singular blight allowed it to directly communicate with the dragon. It was called Velchev, the Mouth of Blighterghast.\n\"What have you done to me?\" Krueger said, rolling over onto his hands and knees. The other cultists had stopped chanting, and the cavern fell into an eerie silence.\n\"Old debts come due, Stormlord, but do not despair. You have been blessed,\" Velchev said. \"You have been chosen to bear the essence of the great one until such time as he can be remade.\"\n\"Blighterghast is . . . slain?\" Krueger asked, one hand cradling his head, his eyes shut against the onslaught of a painfully bright light that only he could see.\n\"You saw the master’s death,\" Velchev said. \"<I>Felt</I> it.\"\n\"How?\"\n\"Much has happened since you’ve been away.\" Velchev’s bestial face twisted in a grimace. \"The Dragonfather has a new ally from across the sea. With this power at his command, he will storm the mainland and take back what he <I>believes</I> is rightfully his.\"",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                ""
            ],
            "colorHex": "",
            "textColorHex": "",
            "mediaPath": "",
            "widthPerc": 100,
            "mediaWidth": 0,
            "mediaHeight": 0,
            "caption": [
