        {
            "guidStr": "e971157b-2da5-45a2-a62d-935aa22bac43",
            "name": [
                "Name",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                ""
            ],
            "isLive": false,
            "metadata": "",
            "deleted": false,
            "type": "Body",
            "topMarginOverride": -1,
            "bottomMarginOverride": -1,
            "leftMarginOverride": -1,
            "rightMarginOverride": -1,
            "title": [
                "",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                ""
            ],
            "body": [
                "The crystal pulsed again, and Krueger clenched his teeth against another vision. He saw a mighty force of soldiers and warjacks gathered from all the varied nations of western Immoren. Dragons soared above the great army, wings outstretched, blotting out sun and sky, casting all into shadow. The vision sparked both hope and horror in Krueger, for he knew what this grand alliance marched toward. On the horizon, Toruk loomed like a mountain given breath and life, and beneath the Dragonfather, a vast swarm of warriors and terrible machines lit by the green balefire and the blood-soaked crimson of Orgoth blaze furnaces waited.\n\"You understand,\" Velchev said, as if he too had seen Blighterghast’s prophetic vision. Perhaps he had.\n\"I understand,\" Krueger said. His old ambitions mingled with the desires of the dragon, and he saw with perfect, awful clarity that even death could not change the course of his fate.\n<I>So much more I wished to accomplish. </I>\n#\nCaptain Madison Calder watched her soldiers strip the barding from Onus’ corpse. A human soldier might be buried in their armor, and it tore at her heart that she could not extend the same dignity to her faithful warhorse.",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                ""
            ],
            "colorHex": "",
            "textColorHex": "",
            "mediaPath": "",
            "widthPerc": 100,
            "mediaWidth": 0,
            "mediaHeight": 0,
            "caption": [
