        },
        {
            "guidStr": "0a83fcde-e0b3-40a9-8258-fabd7b010ec4",
            "name": [
                "Name",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                ""
            ],
            "isLive": false,
            "metadata": "",
            "deleted": false,
            "type": "Body",
            "topMarginOverride": -1,
            "bottomMarginOverride": -1,
            "leftMarginOverride": -1,
            "rightMarginOverride": -1,
            "title": [
                "",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                ""
            ],
            "body": [
                "\"I’m sorry, boy,\" she whispered, then to the four legionnaires carefully removing the destrier’s armor. \"Take him with us. Everyone goes home.\"\nThe battle against the Orgoth had ended only a few short hours ago, and Cygnaran and Khadoran medics with groups of soldiers in tow moved around the colossal corpse of Blighterghast, saving those who could be saved and bearing away the bodies of those who couldn’t. The latter group outnumbered the former ten to one.\nCalder looked out over the scorched landscape. The fierce heat of the caldera radiated up through the cracked earth, creating a shimmer on the horizon, but joining the mirage was a single point of crimson radiance, a lone candle on a vast illusory lake. She pulled her spyglass from her belt and gazed through it.\nA figure wreathed in flame floated slowly toward them, the immense heat from its sizzling corona cracking and buckling the ground beneath it. The fire was so intense, the radiance so blinding, that Calder could not look directly at the approaching figure. Just the same, she knew its appearance so soon after the battle was no coincidence.",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                ""
            ],
            "colorHex": "",
            "textColorHex": "",
