        },
        {
            "guidStr": "3bae8d67-914a-4150-aabf-50dd3c00dc41",
            "name": [
                "Name",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                ""
            ],
            "isLive": false,
            "metadata": "",
            "deleted": false,
            "type": "Body",
            "topMarginOverride": -1,
            "bottomMarginOverride": -1,
            "leftMarginOverride": -1,
            "rightMarginOverride": -1,
            "title": [
                "",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                ""
            ],
            "body": [
                "<I>Blackclad?</I> Calder thought. It made no sense.\n\"I have come to speak with Captain Madison Calder,\" the apparition said, settling on the ground, its nimbus of flames dying away. The voice was loud, bold, and male.\n\"I am she,\" Calder said and spurred her mount forward. \"Who are you?\"\n\"I was once Krueger the Stormlord,\" the figure said, his voice distant, as if the name were little more than a memory. His next words bore the weight of resignation. \"Now I speak for Blighterghast.\"\nCalder knew that name. Krueger had been a mighty blackclad druid who had closed one of the great gates during the Infernal War and had been slain in the process.\n\"Krueger is ten years in his grave,\" Savaryn interjected, jerking his head back toward the mountainous corpse of Blighterghast. \"And the dragon is long past speaking.\"\n\"All is not as it seems,\" Krueger replied. \"Before the Orgoth claimed Blighterghast’s life, the dragon transferred its essence to me.\"\nCalder remembered Blighterghast’s booming voice echoing over the battle, an awful rhythmic chant, like a mighty spell or ritual. It made a horrid kind of sense. \"Then who am I speaking to? Krueger the Stormlord or Blighterghast?\"",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                ""
            ],
