            ],
            "body": [
                "\"Neither,\" Krueger said. \"Both.\"\nCalder shook her head, but a tendril of cold fear crawled up her spine. The absolute authority and confidence with which Krueger spoke unnerved her. \"Even if I believe you are what you say, why have you come?\"\n\"Long ago, Blighterghast and its siblings struck a pact. Should Toruk return, they would stand against him,\" Krueger said. \"I represent that alliance. I come to deliver terms of a further alliance with the nations of western Immoren.\"\n\"What terms?\" Calder said. \"Cygnar has agreed to nothing.\"\n\"Your agreement is not required—only your cooperation.\"\n\"Is that a threat?\" Calder asked.\nFlames burst to life around Krueger, a halo of withering heat. When he spoke again, his words boomed across the hellish landscape, echoing off the clouds and surrounding mountains. It was not the voice of a man; it was the voice of a monster. \"Fool. Do you not understand what has happened? The Orgoth have taken Blighterghast’s <I>athanc</I> for one purpose: to seal an alliance with Toruk and the Empire of Cryx. Together, they will overrun western Immoren, and the Dragonfather will seek to reclaim the <I>athancs</I> of his progeny. Even with all the armies of all the nations of western Immoren at your back, you cannot stand before these enemies.\"",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                ""
            ],
