            ],
            "isLive": false,
            "metadata": "",
            "deleted": false,
            "type": "Body",
            "topMarginOverride": -1,
            "bottomMarginOverride": -1,
            "leftMarginOverride": -1,
            "rightMarginOverride": -1,
            "title": [
                "",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                ""
            ],
            "body": [
                "With perhaps more sense than its rider, Calder’s warhorse retreated from the burning specter. She pulled gently on the reins despite a strong urge to wheel around and flee. When she spoke again, she somehow managed to keep the tremor from her voice. \"I don’t understand. What is it you want?\"\n\"I am not asking for anything,\" Krueger said. \"Henceforth, we shall battle as one. My enemies are your enemies. You will deliver this message to your leaders.\"\n\"You want me to propose an alliance with a blackclad druid who died ten years ago and a dragon I saw slain right here on this battlefield?\" Calder said, sharing a look of disbelief with Savaryn as she spoke the words. She would think the whole thing absurd if she weren’t so terrified. \"What do I even tell them?\"\nKrueger’s reply was immediate and delivered with disturbing stoicism. \"It is simple. They will commit their armies, their people, their blood to my cause. The enemies of Blighterghast will know his wrath.\"",
